The Kernal for Linux responsible for managing files.
System calls - how the application ask the kernel to perform operations
Filesystem - how files and directories are organised and stored

How file move
Layer 1: Application (Initiate but donot change the disk directly)
Layer 2: Sys call, it is the request from an application to the kernal
Layer 3: Virtual Filesystem (example ext4, Btrfs, etc)

How does the linux know when a file is changed?
Linux provides a mechanism called inotify.
It allows the program to ask kernal to notify when something changes.

Difference between (Copy and Move)
Copy -> Delete original file

Will use the Linux notify system.
Problem 1: Notify is not recursive
    solution: use -r flag to make it recursive


